While using Cloudflare KV as storage medium, sometimes the set operation would fail because the expiry TTL ends up being < 60 which is is as under:

```typescript
export function CloudflareStorage(
  options: CloudflareStorageOptions,
): StorageAdapter {
  return {
    async set(key: string[], value: any, expiry?: Date) {
      await options.namespace.put(joinKey(key), JSON.stringify(value), {
        expirationTtl: expiry
          ? Math.floor((expiry.getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000)
          : undefined,
      })
    }
```

The line regarding the computation of TTL needs to include Math.max as under:

```typescript
const expirationTtl: expiry ? Math.max(Math.floor((expiry.getTime() - Date.now()) / 1000), 60) : undefined;
```
and with this one small fix, the error wouldn't happen. I have this modified copy of the whole provider in production and works flawlessly.

Can contribute the PR.

